alve the tomatoes.\nSoften garlic in oil, add squid and tomatoes and simmer gently until the squid is tender.\nBoil pasta until al dente, toss with the sauce and finish with parsley.", "Calories (kcal)": 540.0, "Protein (g)": 30.0, "Carbs (g)": 72.0, "Fat (g)": 14.0, "Fiber (g)": 3.0, "Sugar (g)": 4.0, "Sodium (mg)": 650.0, "Order": 15}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "napoli-spaghetti-alla-puttanesca", "Name": "Spaghetti alla puttanesca", "City ID": "napoli", "Category": "Local Specialties", "Description": "A prepared local dish with a simplified prototype recipe.", "Image URL": "https://cdn77-s3.lazycatkitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/puttanesca-pasta-pan-800x1200.jpg", "Minutes": 25, "Ingredients": "90 g spaghetti\n150 g tomatoes\n25 g olives\n10 g capers\n15 g anchovies\n1 garlic clove\n10 g olive oil", "Steps": "Warm garlic and anchovies in oil until the anchovies break down.\nAdd tomatoes, olives and rinsed capers. Simmer for 15 minutes.\nCook spaghetti until al dente and toss with the sauce and a little pasta water.", "Calories (kcal)": 560.0, "Protein (g)": 18.0, "Carbs (g)": 74.0, "Fat (g)": 21.0, "Fiber (g)": 3.0, "Sugar (g)": 4.0, "Sodium (mg)": 650.0, "Order": 16}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "london-sausage-roll", "Name": "Sausage roll", "City ID": "london", "Category": "Street Food", "Description": "Discover Sausage roll in London. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://thegreatbritishbakeoff.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/newVegan-sausage-rolls_V3-1024x450.jpg", "Minutes": 40, "Ingredients": "70 g puff pastry\n80 g pork sausage meat\nBeaten egg for glazing", "Steps": "Wrap the sausage meat in pastry and seal the seam.\nBrush with egg.\nBake at 200 °C for about 30 minutes until the pastry is golden and the pork filling is fully cooked.", "Calories (kcal)": 540.0, "Protein (g)": 18.0, "Carbs (g)": 37.0, "Fat (g)": 36.0, "Fiber (g)": 2.0, "Sugar (g)": 2.0, "Sodium (mg)": 850.0, "Order": 17}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "london-scotch-egg", "Name": "Scotch egg", "City ID": "london", "Category": "Street Food", "Description": "Discover Scotch egg in London. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://i.redd.it/ierbhjysxje11.jpg", "Minutes": 30, "Ingredients": "1 boiled peeled egg\n80 g sausage meat\n15 g flour\nHalf a beaten egg\n20 g breadcrumbs\nFrying oil", "Steps": "Enclose the boiled egg completely in sausage meat, then coat with flour, beaten egg and breadcrumbs.\nFry gently until golden and the sausage layer is fully cooked throughout.\nDrain before serving.", "Calories (kcal)": 490.0, "Protein (g)": 26.0, "Carbs (g)": 24.0, "Fat (g)": 32.0, "Fiber (g)": 2.0, "Sugar (g)": 2.0, "Sodium (mg)": 760.0, "Order": 18}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "london-fish-and-chips-takeaway-style", "Name": "Fish and chips (takeaway style)", "City ID": "london", "Category": "Street Food", "Description": "Discover Fish and chips (takeaway style) in London. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://www.eatingeurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/Fish_and_chips_at_restaurant_London-2.jpg", "Minutes": 45, "Ingredients": "160 g cod\n200 g potatoes\n30 g flour\nSparkling water\nFrying oil\nLemon", "Steps": "Cut potatoes into chips and fry until cooked and golden.\nMix flour with enough sparkling water to form a light batter.\nDip dry fish in the batter and fry until crisp and cooked through.\nDrain and serve with chips and lemon.", "Calories (kcal)": 690.0, "Protein (g)": 34.0, "Carbs (g)": 72.0, "Fat (g)": 30.0, "Fiber (g)": 5.0, "Sugar (g)": 3.0, "Sodium (mg)": 580.0, "Order": 19}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "london-pork-pie", "Name": "Pork pie", "City ID": "london", "Category": "Street Food", "Description": "Discover Pork pie in London. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://nerdswithknives.com/wp-content/smush-webp/2025/07/IMG_4612-Edit-9-scaled.jpg.webp", "Minutes": 70, "Ingredients": "80 g shortcrust pastry\n100 g minced pork\nThyme\nSalt and pepper\nBeaten egg for glazing", "Steps": "Season the pork.\nLine a small pie tin with pastry, fill with pork and cover with a pastry lid, sealing the edge and making a steam hole.\nBrush with egg and bake at 180 °C for about 45–50 minutes until the filling is cooked through.\nThis is a simple pastry version without jelly.", "Calories (kcal)": 620.0, "Protein (g)": 25.0, "Carbs (g)": 42.0, "Fat (g)": 39.0, "Fiber (g)": 2.0, "Sugar (g)": 2.0, "Sodium (mg)": 720.0, "Order": 20}}]}
