{"typecast": true, "records": [{"fields": {"Dish ID": "london-beef-wellington", "Name": "Beef Wellington", "City ID": "london", "Category": "Local Specialties", "Description": "A prepared local dish with a simplified prototype recipe.", "Image URL": "https://platform.london.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/31/chorus/uploads/chorus_asset/file/19598516/337.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=7.6335877862595,0,84.732824427481,100", "Minutes": 75, "Ingredients": "150 g beef fillet\n100 g mushrooms\n80 g puff pastry\n20 g prosciutto\n5 g mustard\n1 beaten egg\n5 g oil", "Steps": "Sear the beef in oil and allow it to cool. Finely chop and cook mushrooms until their moisture evaporates; cool.\nBrush beef with mustard, wrap in prosciutto and mushroom mixture, then enclose in pastry. Seal and brush with beaten egg.\nBake at 200 °C until the pastry is golden and the beef reaches the desired safe doneness, checking with a thermometer. Rest before slicing.", "Calories (kcal)": 820.0, "Protein (g)": 43.0, "Carbs (g)": 45.0, "Fat (g)": 49.0, "Fiber (g)": 3.0, "Sugar (g)": 4.0, "Sodium (mg)": 650.0, "Order": 31}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "madrid-bocadillo-de-calamares", "Name": "Bocadillo de calamares", "City ID": "madrid", "Category": "Street Food", "Description": "Discover Bocadillo de calamares in Madrid. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://viajarconraul.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/2024-01-26.jpg", "Minutes": 25, "Ingredients": "100 g cleaned squid rings\n80 g baguette\n25 g flour\nFrying oil\nLemon", "Steps": "Prepare the cleaned squid rings, flour, baguette and lemon. If the squid was frozen, thaw it completely in the refrigerator first.\nPat the squid rings thoroughly dry with kitchen paper. Put the flour in a shallow dish and coat the rings lightly, shaking off any excess.\nSplit the baguette lengthways without cutting all the way through. Keep it ready before frying so you can serve the squid while crisp.\nHeat frying oil in a deep, stable pan to about 175–180 °C, using a thermometer. Leave plenty of space above the oil and keep water away from the pan.\nLower a small batch of squid into the oil carefully. Fry until the coating is lightly golden and the squid is opaque and cooked through; do not crowd the pan.\nLift out with a slotted spoon and drain on kitchen paper. Let the oil return to temperature before cooking the next batch.\nFill the baguette with the hot squid, add a squeeze of lemon and serve immediately. Add salt to taste if needed.", "Calories (kcal)": 520.0, "Protein (g)": 26.0, "Carbs (g)": 68.0, "Fat (g)": 17.0, "Fiber (g)": 3.0, "Sugar (g)": 3.0, "Sodium (mg)": 600.0, "Order": 32}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "madrid-empanadas", "Name": "Empanadas", "City ID": "madrid", "Category": "Street Food", "Description": "Discover Empanadas in Madrid. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1b/12/3e/e5/empanadas-malvon-lista.jpg?w=1100&h=1100&s=1", "Minutes": 40, "Ingredients": "80 g shortcrust pastry\n60 g canned tuna\n40 g onion\n60 g tomato\n10 g olives", "Steps": "Cook chopped onion and tomato until thick, then mix with drained tuna and chopped olives.\nFill pastry circles, fold and seal.\nBake at 190 °C for about 25 minutes until golden and hot throughout.", "Calories (kcal)": 500.0, "Protein (g)": 22.0, "Carbs (g)": 43.0, "Fat (g)": 27.0, "Fiber (g)": 4.0, "Sugar (g)": 5.0, "Sodium (mg)": 700.0, "Order": 33}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "madrid-patatas-bravas", "Name": "Patatas bravas", "City ID": "madrid", "Category": "Street Food", "Description": "Discover Patatas bravas in Madrid. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1c/a3/a0/b6/img-20210213-wa0025-largejpg.jpg?w=1100&h=1100&s=1", "Minutes": 40, "Ingredients": "200 g potatoes\n100 g passata\n20 g onion\n15 g olive oil\nSmoked paprika\nChilli", "Steps": "Dice the potatoes, toss with 10 g oil and roast at 220 °C until crisp and tender.\nSoften the onion in the remaining oil, add passata, paprika and chilli and simmer for 10 minutes.\nSpoon over the potatoes.", "Calories (kcal)": 350.0, "Protein (g)": 6.0, "Carbs (g)": 48.0, "Fat (g)": 16.0, "Fiber (g)": 6.0, "Sugar (g)": 8.0, "Sodium (mg)": 410.0, "Order": 34}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "madrid-croquetas-de-jam-n", "Name": "Croquetas de jamón", "City ID": "madrid", "Category": "Street Food", "Description": "Discover Croquetas de jamón in Madrid. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/santerra-mejores-croquetas-jamon-madrid-experta-6822e1953ac82.jpg?crop=0.669xw:1.00xh;0.135xw,0&resize=640:*", "Minutes": 50, "Ingredients": "100 ml milk\n25 g flour\n15 g butter\n30 g cured ham\nHalf a beaten egg\n20 g breadcrumbs\nFrying oil", "Steps": "Cook butter and flour together, gradually whisk in milk and cook until very thick.\nStir in finely chopped ham and chill until firm; chilling time is extra.\nShape into croquettes, coat with beaten egg and breadcrumbs and fry until golden and piping hot inside.", "Calories (kcal)": 460.0, "Protein (g)": 17.0, "Carbs (g)": 37.0, "Fat (g)": 27.0, "Fiber (g)": 2.0, "Sugar (g)": 7.0, "Sodium (mg)": 740.0, "Order": 35}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "madrid-cocido-madrile-o", "Name": "Cocido madrileño", "City ID": "madrid", "Category": "Main Dishes", "Description": "Discover Cocido madrileño in Madrid. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://doeatbetterexperience.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/https3A2F2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com2Fpublic2Fimages2F99fbeaf5-e7b0-4cbc-bf6c-7bab6abe50dc_4284x4830-scaled.jpeg", "Minutes": 150, "Ingredients": "100 g stewing beef\n40 g chorizo\n120 g cooked chickpeas\n100 g potato\n80 g carrot\nWater", "Steps": "Cover the beef with water and simmer gently until tender, about 2 hours, skimming as needed.\nAdd potato, carrot and chorizo and cook until tender.\nAdd