", "Name": "Oreja a la plancha", "City ID": "madrid", "Category": "Main Dishes", "Description": "Discover Oreja a la plancha in Madrid. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://www.cocinayaficiones.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/oreja-al-ajillo-a-la-plancha.3.jpg", "Minutes": 20, "Ingredients": "150 g ready-cooked pig's ear\n5 g olive oil\nGarlic\nParsley\nPaprika", "Steps": "Use fully cooked pig's ear and follow its package preparation instructions.\nSlice into bite-size pieces.\nSear in a hot pan with oil until hot and crisp at the edges, then toss with garlic, parsley and paprika.", "Calories (kcal)": 390.0, "Protein (g)": 27.0, "Carbs (g)": 2.0, "Fat (g)": 30.0, "Fiber (g)": 0.0, "Sugar (g)": 0.0, "Sodium (mg)": 620.0, "Order": 39}}, {"fields": {"Dish ID": "madrid-churros-con-chocolate", "Name": "Churros con chocolate", "City ID": "madrid", "Category": "Sweets", "Description": "Discover Churros con chocolate in Madrid. A simplified preparation is included below.", "Image URL": "https://travelsaroundspain.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/1.jpg", "Minutes": 30, "Ingredients": "50 g flour\n80 ml water\n5 g butter\n10 g sugar\n30 g dark chocolate\n50 ml milk\nFrying oil", "Steps": "Bring water and butter to a boil, stir in flour until a firm paste forms, then cool slightly.\nPipe short strips and fry until golden and cooked through.\nDrain and dust with sugar.\nMelt the chocolate into warm milk and serve as a dipping sauce.", "Calories (kcal)": 480.0, "Protein (g)": 7.0, "Carbs (g)": 60.0, "Fat (g)": 24.0, "Fiber (g)": 4.0, "Sugar (g)": 25.0, "Sodium (mg)": 100.0, "Order": 40}}]}
